<title>UK: Shell active on 13 mln inter-dealer trade.</title>
<headline>Shell active on 13 mln inter-dealer trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in oil company Shell Transport and Trading Plc were the most actively traded in London on Monday after a huge 13.7 million interdealer trade.</p>
<p>The shares were up 4p at 443p in volume of nearly 18-1/2 million by 1135 GMT. The large market maker to market maker trade was recorded at 0914 GMT at a price of 437-1/2p.</p>
<p>&quot;The huge volume was almost certainly against an OTC (over-the-counter) expiry,&quot; said one senior dealer. &quot;But there's no way of knowing for sure.&quot;</p>
<p>Shell is scheduled to report second quarter earnings on Thursday.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
